      "rationale": "Correct answer: Iron, steel, or reinforced concrete. This is directly supported by PD 1096 2004 Revised IRR, Section 1210.",
      "explanation": "The 10.00 sq.m cross-section threshold triggers the ground-frame requirement. For towers below this threshold, the roof structure may be sufficient to resist overturning. The provision is rooted in structural engineering: larger cross-sections catch more wind and generate more seismic mass.",
