      "rationale": "Correct answer: One third of the supporting roof area. This is directly supported by PD 1096 2004 Revised IRR, Section 1210.",
      "explanation": "The two penthouse height limits — 3.60 m for general mechanical penthouses and 8.40 m for elevator/tank enclosures — are the most tested values from Sec. 1210. The critical exam trap is applying the 8.40 m to generator rooms or AHU rooms, which fall under the 3.60 m limit.",
